Track 2: The Cartographer’s Lung
- Story & Context: Mara sits at the center of the rooftop rave, tracing the borders of a dead continent onto a scrap of wet paper with charcoal stolen from a funeral pyre. She ignores the crowd’s chaos, focusing on the way her flute notes blur when the wind pulls the moisture from the air. "I count the borders just to know where I am allowed to go."
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A close-up of a person’s face etched with exhaustion and curiosity, holding a thin, antique wooden flute, glowing bioluminescent water particles floating in the air, melancholic atmosphere.

Track 3: Did You See The Pier Walk Away?
- Story & Context: Old man Halloway swears he watched the entire wooden pier untie its own ropes and drift into the black fog while the music hit its peak. The witnesses say it was just an optical trick caused by the heat and the constant, rhythmic thumping of the sewage-pipe drums against the rooftop concrete. "Did you see the wood surrender to the current's heavy hand?"
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A surreal, haunting image of a wooden boardwalk disintegrating into floating splinters and ropes against an infinite, dark, mirror-like sea, foggy and dreamlike quality.

